This crate (`symphonia-format-spdif`) is a pure-Rust IEC 61937 data burst demuxer. It is licensed
under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia (see `LICENSE`).

Algorithms derived from FFmpeg
------------------------------

The burst framing follows FFmpeg's `libavformat/spdifdec.c` (Copyright (c) 2009 Bartlomiej Wolowiec,
Copyright (c) 2010 Anssi Hannula) and `libavformat/spdif.h` (Copyright (c) 2009 Bartlomiej
Wolowiec): the sync word search, the data type values, the burst repetition periods, the payload
length in bits (bytes for E-AC-3) rounded up to 16 bits, the 16-bit byte swap, and the ADTS
raw data block count. These files are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later. Only the algorithms and constants were reimplemented; no source code was
copied.
